<!-- 03 / Website Audit -->
<div class="showcase-row row align-items-center g-5">

  <!-- Left / Research Narrative -->
  <div class="col-lg-5">
    <p class="description">03 / Website Evaluation</p>

    <h3>Auditing the Existing Digital Experience</h3>

    <p>
      Our team conducted expert evaluations of Neurofit's
      existing marketing website, examining information
      architecture, content clarity, navigation behaviour,
      conversion pathways, and accessibility.
    </p>

    <p>
      My audit identified ambiguous navigation labels,
      unclear audience segmentation, fragmented calls to
      action, and accessibility barriers. Observations
      about navigation and labeling were also echoed in
      our exploratory research with professional stakeholders.
    </p>

    <p>
      Beyond these overlapping findings, the audit highlighted
      opportunities to improve conversion hierarchy and
      establish more accessible, consistent UI patterns.
    </p>

    <p class="showcase-contribution">
      <strong>My Contribution</strong><br>
       UX Audit · Information Architecture
      Evaluation · CTA Strategy Assessment ·
      Accessibility Review · Prioritized Recommendations
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Right / Selected Findings -->
  <div class="col-lg-7">
    <div class="nf-research-panel nf-audit-showcase">

      <span>WEBSITE AUDIT / SELECTED FINDINGS</span>

      <h4>Identifying Experience Barriers</h4>

      <!-- Finding 01 -->
      <div class="nf-audit-finding">

        <div class="nf-audit-finding-label">
          01 / CONVERSION DESIGN
        </div>

        <h5>Fragmented CTA Strategy</h5>

        <p>
          Multiple calls to action directed visitors toward
          similar sign-up or demo-booking flows, without
          clearly distinguishing user intent, professional
          audience, or readiness to engage.
        </p>

        <div class="nf-audit-opportunity">
          <strong>DESIGN OPPORTUNITY</strong>
          <p>
            Introduce progressive conversion pathways
            with clearer CTA labels and actions aligned
            with different stages of the decision journey.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Finding 02 -->
      <div class="nf-audit-finding">

        <div class="nf-audit-finding-label">
          02 / ACCESSIBILITY
        </div>

        <h5>Accessibility &amp; Interface Barriers</h5>

        <div class="nf-audit-score">
          <strong>87</strong>
          <span>
            Lighthouse accessibility score<br>
            Original website
          </span>
        </div>

        <p>
          The audit identified insufficient colour contrast,
          unclear accessible link names, small text, and
          inconsistent language settings across pages.
        </p>

        <div class="nf-audit-opportunity">
          <strong>DESIGN OPPORTUNITY</strong>
          <p>
            Improve colour contrast, text legibility,
            semantic labelling, and accessibility
            consistency across reusable UI components.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="nf-visual-caption">
        Selected findings from our website audit.
        Lighthouse results informed the accessibility review
        but do not represent a comprehensive WCAG assessment.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>

</div>


