<div class="showcase-row row align-items-center g-5">

  <!-- Left: Research Narrative -->
  <div class="col-lg-5">
    <p class="description">05 / Behavioural Analytics</p>

    <h3>Connecting Website Behaviour to Design Strategy</h3>

    <p>
      I independently analyzed Neurofit's Google Analytics 4
      data to evaluate page performance, audience engagement,
      and content effectiveness across the existing website.
    </p>

    <p>
      Engagement with clinician-focused content, FAQs,
      company information, and outcomes-related articles
      suggested opportunities to better support professional
      visitors' information needs. In contrast, the
      insurer-focused page received limited engagement,
      raising questions about its visibility and relevance.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also identified gaps in CTA and sign-up conversion
      tracking. To support future redesign evaluation,
      I proposed custom GA4 events, improved sign-up
      measurement, and a KPI framework covering engagement
      and conversion performance.
    </p>

    <p class="showcase-contribution">
      <strong>My Contribution</strong><br>
      Independent GA4 Analysis · Audience & Content Insights ·
      Conversion Tracking Assessment · KPI Framework ·
      UX & Business Recommendations
