<section class="feature-development-section project-section project-section--dark nf-execution-section" id="ui-design">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row mb-5"><div class="col-lg-9">
      <p class="description">05 / Design Response &amp; UI Execution</p>
      <h2>From research insights to a scalable experience</h2>
      <p class="feature-development-intro">As the project's UI Technical Art Director, I led the creation of a reusable design system and designed key responsive interfaces. Our approach connected research-informed content decisions with a warm, modern visual language, audience-specific communication, and implementation-ready patterns.</p>
    </div></div>

    <!-- 01 CREATIVE DIRECTION -->
    <div class="row align-items-center g-5 feature-development-row">
      <div class="col-lg-5">
        <span class="feature-detail-number">01</span>
        <h3>Setting a visual direction that builds trust</h3>
        <p>Guided by four keywords — Warm, Neuroscience-Inspired, Alive, and Accurate — we aimed for a visual identity that felt approachable and credible without appearing overly clinical.</p>
        <p>I analyzed competitors' colour palettes and visual language, while two teammates gathered inspiration references. Together, we established the colour direction, which I translated into reusable UI components and design patterns.</p>
        <div class="feature-detail-point"><h4>Design rationale</h4><p>Purple became the visual anchor, supported by restrained accents, neutral surfaces, and selective gradients to reduce visual competition and guide attention.</p></div>
